questions.stem:
A warehouse scanner beeps once for each pallet slot it visits, and the loop bound is written as less than or equal. What does the printer output?
for (int i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {
    System.out.print(i);
}

A ticket dispenser counts only the odd-numbered coupons, and the counter jumps by two each pass. How many coupons does it process?
int coupons = 0;
for (int i = 1; i < 5; i = i + 2) {
    coupons++;
}

A signal booster doubles its gain every tick until it is loud enough, so the pass count is not known in advance. How many ticks are counted?
int value = 1;
int ticks = 0;
while (value < 20) {
    value = value * 2;
    ticks++;
}
System.out.println(ticks);

A cashier sums the prices of the first four tickets. What prints?
int total = 0;
for (int i = 1; i <= 4; i++) {
    total = total + i;
}
System.out.println(total);

A shift total is meant to add up every pallet, but the running value was declared inside the loop body. What prints?
int total = 0;
for (int i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {
    int running = 0;
    running = running + i;
    total = running;
}
System.out.println(total);

A retry budget is spent one attempt at a time, and the loop spends the last one before failing. How many attempts run?
int retries = 5;
int attempts = 0;
while (retries-- > 0) {
    attempts++;
}
System.out.println(attempts);

A music player sums the first three tracks, and its counter is advanced inside the body with nothing in the update slot. What prints?
int sum = 0;
for (int i = 1; ; i++) {
    if (i > 3) break;
    sum = sum + i;
}
System.out.println(sum);

A till rolls a running total until the cashier enters the terminator value. What prints?
java.util.Scanner in = new java.util.Scanner("3 7 0 9");
int total = 0;
int n = in.nextInt();
while (n != 0) {
    total = total + n;
    n = in.nextInt();
}
System.out.println(total);

A login prompt insists on one attempt before it will check the user's answer. How many attempts are counted?
int n = 0;
int attempts = 0;
do {
    attempts++;
    n = n + 1;
} while (n < 0);
System.out.println(attempts);

An import routine sums every number in a token stream, relying on the reader to report when it is empty. What prints?
java.util.Scanner in = new java.util.Scanner("4 8 15");
int total = 0;
while (in.hasNextInt()) {
    total = total + in.nextInt();
}
System.out.println(total);

A shelf scanner stops looking at a shelf as soon as it finds a defect, but it keeps scanning the rest of the shelves. How many shelves does it inspect?
int hits = 0;
for (int r = 1; r <= 2; r++) {
    for (int c = 1; c <= 3; c++) {
        if (c == 2) break;
        hits++;
    }
}
System.out.println(hits);

A search over ordered pairs stops the whole search, not just the inner pass, once it finds the target product. How many pairs are examined?
int pairs = 0;
outer:
for (int a = 1; a <= 4; a++) {
    for (int b = 1; b <= 4; b++) {
        if (a * b == 6) break outer;
        pairs++;
    }
}
System.out.println(pairs);

A device draws four units of power per tick and loses three, and the loop runs until the level would go below twenty. How many minutes pass?
int battery = 78;
int minutes = 0;
while (battery > 20) {
    minutes = minutes + 4;
    battery = battery - 3;
}
System.out.println(minutes);

A fuzz tester has a continue inside a while loop with the increment written in the body. What does this loop do?
int i = 0;
int spins = 0;
while (i < 3) {
    spins++;
    if (i == 1) continue;
    i++;
}
System.out.println(spins);

A launch timer counts down from three, and the digits are appended with no separator. What prints?
String countdown = "";
for (int s = 3; s >= 1; s--) {
    countdown = countdown + s;
}
System.out.println(countdown);

A reporter prints the counter after its loop, and the header declared the counter separately. What prints?
int sum = 0;
int i = 1;
for (; i <= 4; i++) {
    sum = sum + i;
}
System.out.println(i);

A report tries to read its counter after the loop, but the counter was declared in the loop header. What happens?
for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
}
System.out.println(i);

A grid walks every row and every column of a small tray. How many cells does the counter visit?
int cells = 0;
for (int s = 1; s <= 3; s++) {
    for (int t = 1; t <= 4; t++) {
        cells++;
    }
}
System.out.println(cells);

A librarian counts only the even-numbered positions on every shelf, so the counter sits inside a filter. How many positions are counted?
int shelves = 3;
int booksPerShelf = 4;
int tall = 0;
for (int s = 0; s < shelves; s++) {
    for (int b = 0; b < booksPerShelf; b++) {
        if (b % 2 == 0) {
            tall = tall + 1;
        }
    }
}
System.out.println(tall);

A report joins the first three order numbers with commas, appending the separator inside the loop. What prints?
String codes = "";
for (int i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {
    codes = codes + i + ",";
}
System.out.println(codes);

A checksum routine adds the digits of an order number by peeling off the last digit each pass. What prints?
int n = 408;
int sum = 0;
while (n > 0) {
    sum = sum + n % 10;
    n = n / 10;
}
System.out.println(sum);

A promo loop lowers its ceiling after the first two passes, and the condition reads the variable each time. How many passes run?
int limit = 8;
int count = 0;
for (int v = 0; v < limit; v = v + 2) {
    count++;
    if (count == 2) {
        limit = 5;
    }
}
System.out.println(count);

A scheduler reduces two tile counts to their greatest common divisor. What prints?
int a = 48;
int b = 18;
while (b != 0) {
    int t = b;
    b = a % b;
    a = t;
}
System.out.println(a);

A stock report sums every bin, but the loop bound was written with less than or equal. What happens?
int[] stock = {4, 7, 2};
int total = 0;
for (int i = 0; i <= stock.length; i++) {
    total = total + stock[i];
}
System.out.println(total);

A helper method reports the position of the first reading above the cap, and it uses return from inside its loop. What prints?
System.out.println(firstOver(new int[]{3, 9, 14}, 10));
}
static int firstOver(int[] values, int cap) {
    for (int i = 0; i < values.length; i++) {
        if (values[i] > cap) {
            return i;
        }
    }
    return -1;
}

A sensor scan advances only while it is inside the array and the reading is still positive. How many readings are seen?
int[] readings = {5, -1, 7, 8};
int seen = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < readings.length && readings[i] > 0; i++) {
    seen++;
}
System.out.println(seen);

An audit sums every entry except the one with the value 2. What prints?
int skipped = 0;
for (int i = 1; i <= 4; i++) {
    if (i == 2) {
        continue;
    }
    skipped = skipped + i;
}
System.out.println(skipped);

A queue length is totalled with a while loop whose increment sits in the body. What prints?
int total = 0;
int i = 0;
while (i < 4) {
    total = total + i;
    i++;
}
System.out.println(total);

A retried upload counts its attempts, but the code also bumps the counter inside the body. How many passes run?
int passes = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
    passes++;
    i++;
}
System.out.println(passes);

A dial advances in tenths until it passes nought nine, and the accumulated value is printed. What prints?
double v = 0.0;
int steps = 0;
while (v < 0.9 && steps < 12) {
    v = v + 0.1;
    steps++;
}
System.out.println(v);
